Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `s` moves out of a lambda that can run more than once
  --> tests/ui/lambda_move_capture_repeated_call.jet:9:47
    |
  9 |     xs.fold(0, fn(acc, x) { acc + x + consume(s.move()) })
    |                                               ^
  --> tests/ui/lambda_move_capture_repeated_call.jet:9:16
    |
  9 |     xs.fold(0, fn(acc, x) { acc + x + consume(s.move()) })
    |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this lambda may run more than once
 Why: The lambda is passed on or stored, so it may be called again, and that call would use `s` after the first call gave it away
 Fix: Pass a copy (`s.copy()`), or move `s` in as a parameter of the lambda instead of capturing it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
